{%- comment -%}
  Native new-PDP configurator.

  A fork of snippets/product-options.liquid rendering the Figma layout
  server-side. Only the structure is ours: every per-option input still comes
  from the same product-option-accordion / custom-color-picker snippets, so
  product-custom-options.js and product-form-with-options.js bind to the same
  hooks and build the same line-item payload. Nothing here re-implements
  pricing or cart data.

  Differences from the live snippet:
    - no dark "Configure your order here." bar, no circled step numbers (the
      ordering indices are still computed — they drive the CSS `order` that
      places colours / warranty / assembly)
    - groups presented elsewhere in this template are marked
      .pdp-new--card-covered at render time rather than by script, avoiding a
      flash of live-styled options on load. HIDDEN, never skipped: the inputs
      stay in the DOM and live, so nothing leaves the purchase path.

  Accepts:
    - product: {Object} product object (required)
    - section_id: {String} section id for the wrapper (optional, defaults to section.id)
    - installation_match: {String} lowercase needle matched against an option
      group's title; that group is presented as the Figma delivery dropdown
      instead, so it is hidden here (optional)
{%- endcomment -%}

{% liquid
  assign options = product.metafields.options.product_options.value
  if product.selected_or_first_available_variant.metafields.options.product_options.value != blank
    assign options = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.metafields.options.product_options.value
  endif

  if section_id == blank
    assign section_id = section.id
  endif
  assign installation_needle = installation_match | downcase | strip

  assign quantity_index = 0
  assign warranty_index = 1
  assign color_index = 1
  assign assambly_index = 0
  assign visible_total = 0
  assign has_warranty_visible = false
  assign title_downcase = product.title | downcase
  if title_downcase contains 'remanufactured'
    assign color_index = 2
  endif
  assign index = color_index
  assign last_index = index
  assign has_color_option = false
  comment
    Whether a real colour PICKER renders, tested exactly as the render loop
    tests it (product-option title, not category title). has_color_option above
    matches on the category title instead, so the two can disagree — a category
    called "Frame Finish" holding a "Paint Color" option, or one called "Colors"
    holding none. The colours container below is emitted off this flag, so it is
    never rendered empty (an empty flex child would add a phantom column gap).
  endcomment
  assign pdp_has_color_group = false

  for category in options
    assign category_title_downcase = category.title | downcase
    if category_title_downcase contains 'color' or category_title_downcase contains 'colors'
      assign has_color_option = true
    endif
    assign color_title = ''
    assign hidden_option = false
    for product_option in category.product_options.value
      assign title = product_option.product_option_title | downcase
      if title == 'paint color' or title == 'paint colors' or title == 'color' or title == 'vinyl colors' or title == 'vinyl color'
        assign color_title = product_option.product_option_title
        assign pdp_has_color_group = true
      else
        assign color_title = ''
      endif
      if product_option.hide_values
        assign hidden_option = true
      endif
    endfor
    unless category.hide_option
      unless hidden_option
        if color_title == '' and category_title_downcase != 'warranty'
          assign last_index = last_index | plus: 1
        endif
        assign visible_total = visible_total | plus: 1
        if category_title_downcase == 'warranty'
          assign has_warranty_visible = true
        endif
      endunless
    endunless
    assign assambly_index = last_index
  endfor
%}
<div id="Product-Options-{{ section_id }}">
  <product-customization-options
    data-product-id="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
    class="product-options"
    data-product="default"
  >
    {% liquid
      unless has_color_option
        assign index = 0
        assign assambly_index = assambly_index | minus: 1
      endunless
      assign quantity_option = false

      comment
        The colour group is presented at the TOP of the buy box (Sagi, Aug 25),
        above the info tabs, while the remaining groups keep their place below
        the price. It cannot simply be moved out: product-custom-options.js
        scopes its price maths to `this`, so a colour picker outside
        <product-customization-options> would stop contributing its price
        adjustment to the configured total while still reaching the cart.

        So the element stays whole and the groups are emitted into two sibling
        containers instead. The wrappers are display:contents (pdp-new.css), so
        those containers become flex items of .pdp-new__info and the colours one
        can be ordered on its own. Everything stays inside the custom element,
        inside #Product-Options-<id>, and inside #MainProduct-<id>: the variant
        swap, the price maths and the cart payload are all untouched.

        Two passes over the same loop rather than one pass into two buffers:
        the per-category index maths is stateful, so it has to run for EVERY
        category in each pass and only the OUTPUT is filtered. Snapshot the
        starting values so the second pass computes exactly what the first did.
      endcomment
      assign index_init = index
      assign color_index_init = color_index
      assign quantity_index_init = quantity_index
      assign assambly_index_init = assambly_index
      assign pdp_passes = 'colors,rest' | split: ','
      unless pdp_has_color_group
        assign pdp_passes = 'rest' | split: ','
      endunless
    %}

    {%- for pdp_pass in pdp_passes -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign index = index_init
        assign color_index = color_index_init
        assign quantity_index = quantity_index_init
        assign assambly_index = assambly_index_init
        assign quantity_option = false
      -%}
      <div class="pdp-new__opt-{{ pdp_pass }}">
    {% for category in options %}
      {% liquid
        assign color_counter = 0
        assign color_title = ''
        assign color_group = ''
        assign category_title_downcase = category.title | downcase
        assign hidden_option = false

        for product_option in category.product_options.value
          assign title = product_option.product_option_title | downcase
          if title == 'paint color' or title == 'paint colors' or title == 'color' or title == 'vinyl colors' or title == 'vinyl color'
            assign color_counter = color_counter | plus: 1
            assign color_title = product_option.product_option_title
            assign color_group = title | handleize
          else
            assign color_title = ''
          endif
          if product_option.hide_values
            assign hidden_option = true
          endif
          if product_option.option_type == 'Quantity input'
            assign quantity_option = true
          else
            assign quantity_option = false
          endif
        endfor
        unless category.hide_option
          unless hidden_option
            if color_title == '' and category_title_downcase != 'warranty' and category_title_downcase != 'assembly & room of choice installation needed?'
              assign index = index | plus: 1
            endif
          endunless
        endunless
        if index == assambly_index
          assign index = index | minus: 1
        endif

        if quantity_option
          assign quantity_index = 1
          assign color_index = color_index | plus: 1
        endif

        comment
          Which groups this template presents somewhere else.

          Accessory categories are NO LONGER covered here (Tim, Aug 2). The
          add-on cards below the buy box are true linked products on their own
          cart lines, not a view of these inputs, so hiding a configurator
          category because a related product is also sold as an upsell would
          simply remove a purchasable option. Every category now renders.

          The installation group remains covered: it is genuinely re-presented,
          as the Figma "Delivery & Installation Options" dropdown, which drives
          this same input. That is a relocation, not a removal.
        endcomment
        assign pdp_covered = false

        if installation_needle != blank
          for product_option in category.product_options.value
            assign po_title_dc = product_option.product_option_title | downcase
            if po_title_dc contains installation_needle
              assign pdp_covered = true
              break
            endif
          endfor
        endif

        comment
          Which of the two containers this category belongs to. color_counter is
          the render loop's own count of colour pickers in this category, so the
          split matches exactly what gets rendered.
        endcomment
        assign pdp_in_pass = false
        if pdp_pass == 'colors' and color_counter > 0
          assign pdp_in_pass = true
        elsif pdp_pass == 'rest' and color_counter == 0
          assign pdp_in_pass = true
        endif

        comment
          "Accessories / Add Ons" reads as a redundant bucket label above the
          option rows and is dropped (Sagi, Aug 25). Matched on a punctuation-
          and space-stripped title so "Accessories/Add-Ons" and
          "Accessories & Add Ons" are caught too. The label row is hidden in CSS
          rather than skipped here: it carries [data-group-color-name], which
          product-form-with-options.js reads for the cart properties, so it has
          to stay in the DOM. Only this bucket - sibling groups such as "Cable
          Attachments" keep their label.
        endcomment
        assign pdp_title_key = category.title | downcase | replace: '&', '' | replace: '/', '' | replace: '-', '' | replace: ' ', '' | strip
        assign pdp_hide_title = false
        if pdp_title_key == 'accessoriesaddons'
          assign pdp_hide_title = true
        endif
      %}

      {%- if pdp_in_pass -%}
      <div
        class="product-option__item{% if pdp_covered %} pdp-new--card-covered{% endif %}"
        {% unless category.hide_option %}
          style="order:  {% if color_title != blank %}{{ color_index }}{% elsif category_title_downcase == 'warranty' %}{{ warranty_index }}{% elsif category_title_downcase == 'assembly & room of choice installation needed?' %}{{ assambly_index }}{% elsif quantity_option %}0{% else %}{{ index }}{% endif %};"
        {% endunless %}
      >
        {% if category.title != blank %}
          {% comment %} Option-group label - kept as a styled div, not a heading, so it
             doesn't add UI heading tags to the PDP outline (SEO heading QA). The live
             snippet renders a circled step number here; the Figma design has none. {% endcomment %}
          <div
            class="product-options__category-title{% if pdp_hide_title %} pdp-new--title-hidden{% endif %}"
            {% if color_counter == 1 %}
              data-group-color-name="{{ color_group }}"
              data-color-name-title="{{ color_title }}"
            {% endif %}
            {% if category.hide_option %}
              style="display: none !important"
            {% endif %}
          >
            {{- category.title }}
            {% if category.help_text.value != blank %}
              {% render 'related-products-button',
                product_id: product.id,
                product_handle: product.handle,
                product_category: product.metafields.custom.option_category_id.value,
                option_title: category.title
              %}
            {% else %}
              {% for product_option in category.product_options.value %}
                {% if product_option.option_type == 'Select' and product_option.help_text.value != blank %}
                  {% render 'related-products-button',
                    product_id: product.id,
                    product_handle: product.handle,
                    product_category: product.metafields.custom.option_category_id.value,
                    option_title: product_option.product_option_title
                  %}
                  {% break %}
                {% endif %}
              {% endfor %}
            {% endif %}
            {% if color_counter == 1 %}
              {% for product_option in category.product_options.value %}
                {% assign title = product_option.product_option_title | downcase %}
                {% if title == 'paint color' or title == 'paint colors' or title == 'color' or title == 'vinyl colors' or title == 'vinyl color' %}
                  {% if product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.id %}
                    {% render 'related-products-button',
                      product_id: product.id,
                      product_handle: product.handle,
                      product_category: product.metafields.custom.option_category_id.value,
                      option_title: product_option.product_option_title
                    %}
                    <div class="option_selected-container" data-selected-color-option="{{ title | handleize }}">
                      <div class="option_selected" data-option-id="{{ product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.id }}">
                        <div data-color-selected-title>
                          {{ product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.title }}
                        </div>
                        <div class="option_selected-price">
                          {% if product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.price > 0 %}
                            {{ product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.price }}
                          {% endif %}
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    {% break %}
                  {% endif %}
                {% endif %}
              {% endfor %}
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        {% endif %}
        <div class="product-options__category-notification"></div>
        {% for product_option in category.product_options.value %}
          {% assign title = product_option.product_option_title | downcase %}
          {% if title == 'paint color' or title == 'paint colors' or title == 'color' %}
            {% if product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.id %}
              {% assign default = product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.id %}
            {% endif %}
            {% render 'custom-color-picker',
              product: product_option.product_option_variants.value,
              products: product_option,
              default: default,
              color_type: 'paint',
              title: category.title,
              color_counter: color_counter
            %}
          {% endif %}
          {% if title == 'vinyl color' or title == 'vinyl colors' %}
            {% if product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.id %}
              {% assign default = product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.id %}
            {% endif %}
            {% render 'custom-color-picker',
              product: product_option.product_option_variants.value,
              products: product_option,
              default: default,
              color_type: 'vinyl',
              title: category.title,
              color_counter: color_counter
            %}
          {% endif %}
          {% if title != 'paint color' and title != 'vinyl color' and title != 'paint colors' and title != 'vinyl colors' %}
            {% if product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.id %}
              {% assign default = product_option.product_option_sets_default.value.id %}
            {% endif %}
            {% render 'product-option-accordion', category: category, default: default, product_option: product_option, forloop_index: forloop.index, product_id: product.id %}
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {% endfor %}
      {%- comment -%} Once only, in the groups container - these carry ids. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if pdp_pass == 'rest' -%}
        <div
          id="product-options-total-add"
          class="product-options__total-add product-options__total-add--hide"
        >
          Selection will add
          <span
            id="product-options-totalpriceadd"
            class="product-options__total-price-add"
            >$0.00</span
          >
          to the price
        </div>
        <input type="hidden" value="0" class="product-options__total-addcharge">
      {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </product-customization-options>
</div>
